        <h2>The method</h2>
        <p>The desk works from primary sources: filings, disclosures, governance records, and official releases — read in the language they publish in, including Japanese- and Korean-language documents that rarely make it into English-language coverage. Secondary reporting is a pointer to a document, never a substitute for it. <em>TODO: rewrite in own voice — describe the actual daily reading routine.</em></p>
        <p>Every research record separates findings from position. Findings are sourced and checkable; they should hold regardless of who assembled them. A record isn't published until the findings exist and a position is taken. <em>TODO: rewrite in own voice.</em></p>

        <h2>Why positions are signed</h2>
        <p>Analysis without a stated view is easy to write and impossible to grade. Positions here are signed by name and dated so they can be checked later — and be wrong in public. When one is wrong, the correction is published in place with the original text preserved. <em>TODO: rewrite in own voice.</em></p>

        <p>Independence and holdings disclosure are covered on the <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure page</a>. The desk can be reached at <a href="mailto:research@earlylayers.xyz">research@earlylayers.xyz</a>.</p>
